< PAX playground: pax px54 39f8597 + px56 b32a791 (19f24e8), wolf 0.2.33, pelt 90d7c64, boreutils cc64f68.
< pelt is pid 1 with job control (sh -i -m). Try: ls -l /bin, jobs, Ctrl-Z, bg, fg,
< kill %1, timeout, su pax, play mambo. exit (or Ctrl-D) halts the machine.
< lope 5ac37df jumps (its hook in /etc/shrc): cd /etc, cd /bin, then etc alone,
< g -, g, gi, lope list. Its store is in memory, gone at the next boot.
---
> PAX playground: pax px57 120e36b, wolf 0.2.34, pelt 90d7c64, boreutils cc64f68, lope 5ac37df,
> aspen 103ba46, lupin 0.1.55 (static musl). pelt is pid 1 with job control (sh -i -m).
> Try: ls -l /bin, jobs, Ctrl-Z, bg, fg, kill %1, timeout, su pax, play mambo.
> lope jumps (its hook in /etc/shrc): cd /etc, cd /bin, then etc alone, g -, gi.
> aspen is tree(1) in wolf: aspen /, aspen -a -L 2 /home/pax, aspen -J /bin, aspen --du /usr.
> lupin runs wolf programs: cd /usr/share/lupin; lupin run hello.lu (or write one: cat > x.lu).
> Files and lope's store are in memory, gone at the next boot. exit (or Ctrl-D) halts.
46a49
> for t in user/lupin/*.lu; do args+=(/usr/share/lupin/${t##*/}=$t:644); done
